<section id="S8" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">VIII </span><span id="S8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Appendix</span></h2>

<section id="S8.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S8.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">VIII-A</span> </span><span id="S8.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Kalman Filter Dynamics</span></h3>

<div id="S8.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the linear Gaussian dynamics (<a href="#S5.E31" title="Equation 31 ‣ V-B1 Multi-Target Filtering ‣ V-B Deriving the Covertness Bound from Tracking Dynamics ‣ V Extended Example. Detecting and Identifying Pareto-efficient Coordination amongst UAVs ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>), (<a href="#S5.E32" title="Equation 32 ‣ V-B1 Multi-Target Filtering ‣ V-B Deriving the Covertness Bound from Tracking Dynamics ‣ V Extended Example. Detecting and Identifying Pareto-efficient Coordination amongst UAVs ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>).
Based on observations <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{i}_{1},\dots,y^{i}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{i}_{1},\dots,y^{i}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> associated to target <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, the tracking functionality in the radar computes the target <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> state posterior</p>
<table id="S8.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k}^{i}=\mathcal{N}(\hat{x}_{k}^{i},\Sigma_{k}^{i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k}^{i}=\mathcal{N}(\hat{x}_{k}^{i},\Sigma_{k}^{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}_{k}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}_{k}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the conditional mean state estimate and <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{k}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{k}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the covariance, computed by the classical Kalman filter:</p>
<table id="S8.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\Sigma_{k+1|k}^{i}&amp;=A^{i}\Sigma_{k}^{i}(A^{i})^{\top}+Q_{t}(\beta_{t}^{i})\\
K_{k+1}^{i}&amp;=C^{i}\Sigma_{k+1|k}^{i}(C^{i})^{\top}+R_{t}(\alpha_{t})\\
\hat{x}_{k+1}^{i}&amp;=A^{i}\hat{x}^{i}\\
&amp;\quad+\Sigma_{k+1|k}^{i}(C^{i})^{\top}(K^{i}_{k+1|k})^{-1}(y^{i}_{k+1}-C^{i}A^{i}\hat{x}^{i}_{k})\\
\Sigma^{i}_{k+1}&amp;=\Sigma^{i}_{k+1|k}-\Sigma^{i}_{k+1|k}(C^{i})^{\top}(K_{k+1}^{i})^{-1}C^{i}\Sigma^{i}_{k+1|k}\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\Sigma_{k+1|k}^{i}&amp;=A^{i}\Sigma_{k}^{i}(A^{i})^{\top}+Q_{t}(\beta_{t}^{i})\\
K_{k+1}^{i}&amp;=C^{i}\Sigma_{k+1|k}^{i}(C^{i})^{\top}+R_{t}(\alpha_{t})\\
\hat{x}_{k+1}^{i}&amp;=A^{i}\hat{x}^{i}\\
&amp;\quad+\Sigma_{k+1|k}^{i}(C^{i})^{\top}(K^{i}_{k+1|k})^{-1}(y^{i}_{k+1}-C^{i}A^{i}\hat{x}^{i}_{k})\\
\Sigma^{i}_{k+1}&amp;=\Sigma^{i}_{k+1|k}-\Sigma^{i}_{k+1|k}(C^{i})^{\top}(K_{k+1}^{i})^{-1}C^{i}\Sigma^{i}_{k+1|k}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Under the assumption that the model parameters in (<a href="#S5.E31" title="Equation 31 ‣ V-B1 Multi-Target Filtering ‣ V-B Deriving the Covertness Bound from Tracking Dynamics ‣ V Extended Example. Detecting and Identifying Pareto-efficient Coordination amongst UAVs ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>) satisfy <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[A^{i},C^{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[A^{i},C^{i}]</annotation></semantics></math> is detectable and <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[A^{i},\sqrt{Q_{t}(\alpha_{t})}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[A^{i},\sqrt{Q_{t}(\alpha_{t})}]</annotation></semantics></math> is stabilizable, the asymptotic predicted covariance <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{i}_{k+1|k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{i}_{k+1|k}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> is the unique non-negative definite solution of the <span id="S8.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">algebraic Riccati equation</span> (ARE):</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S8.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\mathcal{A}(\alpha_{t},\beta_{t}^{i},\Sigma):=\\
&amp;-\Sigma+A^{i}(\Sigma-\Sigma(C^{i})^{\top}[C^{i}\Sigma(C^{i})^{\top}+R_{t}(\alpha_{t})]^{-1}C^{i}\Sigma)(A^{i})^{\top}\\
&amp;+Q_{t}(\beta_{t}^{i})=0\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\mathcal{A}(\alpha_{t},\beta_{t}^{i},\Sigma):=\\
&amp;-\Sigma+A^{i}(\Sigma-\Sigma(C^{i})^{\top}[C^{i}\Sigma(C^{i})^{\top}+R_{t}(\alpha_{t})]^{-1}C^{i}\Sigma)(A^{i})^{\top}\\
&amp;+Q_{t}(\beta_{t}^{i})=0\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S8.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{t}^{*}(\alpha_{t},\beta_{t}^{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{t}^{*}(\alpha_{t},\beta_{t}^{i})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the solution of the ARE and <math id="S8.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{t}^{*-1}(\alpha_{t},\beta_{t}^{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{t}^{*-1}(\alpha_{t},\beta_{t}^{i})</annotation></semantics></math> be its inverse, representing the asymptotic measurement <span id="S8.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">precision</span> obtained by the radar.</p>
</div>
<section id="S8.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S8.SS1.SSS1.6" class="ltx_text">VIII-A</span>1 </span>Extracting a Covertness Bound</h4>

<div id="S8.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By Lemma 3 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>, we can represent a limit <math id="S8.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Sigma}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Sigma}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> on the radar’s precision of target <math id="S8.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> measurement, <math id="S8.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{t}^{*-1}(\alpha_{t},\beta_{t}^{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{t}^{*-1}(\alpha_{t},\beta_{t}^{i})</annotation></semantics></math> as the simple linear inequality <math id="S8.SS1.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}^{\top}\beta_{t}^{i}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}^{\top}\beta_{t}^{i}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</p>
<table id="S8.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}^{\top}\beta_{t}^{i}\leq 1\Longleftrightarrow\Sigma_{t}^{*-1}(\alpha_{t},\beta_{t}^{i})\leq\bar{\Sigma}^{-1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}^{\top}\beta_{t}^{i}\leq 1\Longleftrightarrow\Sigma_{t}^{*-1}(\alpha_{t},\beta_{t}^{i})\leq\bar{\Sigma}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS1.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the constant <math id="S8.SS1.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> bound is taken without loss of generality. The key idea behind this equivalence is to show the asymptotic precision <math id="S8.SS1.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{*-1}_{n}(\cdot,\beta_{t}^{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{*-1}_{n}(\cdot,\beta_{t}^{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is monotone increasing in the first argument <math id="S8.SS1.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> using the information Kalman filter formulation. Then, we can represent a constraint on the radar’s average precision over measurements of all targets as</p>
<table id="S8.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}^{\top}(\sum_{i=1}^{M}\beta_{t}^{i})\leq 1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}^{\top}(\sum_{i=1}^{M}\beta_{t}^{i})\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS1.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Thus, we recover a direct correspondence between the radar’s average measurement precision and the linear inequality constraint in (<a href="#S5.E29" title="Equation 29 ‣ Definition 5 (Covert Multi-UAV Coordination). ‣ V-A Multi-UAV Covert Coordination Definition ‣ V Extended Example. Detecting and Identifying Pareto-efficient Coordination amongst UAVs ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>). Thus, again, "collective rationality" (<a href="#S5.E29" title="Equation 29 ‣ Definition 5 (Covert Multi-UAV Coordination). ‣ V-A Multi-UAV Covert Coordination Definition ‣ V Extended Example. Detecting and Identifying Pareto-efficient Coordination amongst UAVs ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>) on the part of the UAV network can directly be interpreted as the high-level constrained multi-objective optimization (<a href="#S5.E28" title="Equation 28 ‣ V-A Multi-UAV Covert Coordination Definition ‣ V Extended Example. Detecting and Identifying Pareto-efficient Coordination amongst UAVs ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S8.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S8.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">VIII-B</span> </span><span id="S8.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Lemma 1 Statement and Proof</span></h3>

<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the multi-objective optimization problem (<a href="#S2.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ Definition 3 (Coordinated System). ‣ II-B Coordinated Multi-Agent Systems ‣ II Background. Constrained Multi-Objective Optimization in Coordinated Systems ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>). If <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}^{i}&gt;0\ \forall i\in[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.667em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}^{i}&gt;0\ \forall i\in[M]</annotation></semantics></math> then, letting <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{E}(\{f^{i}\}_{i=1}^{M},\alpha_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{E}(\{f^{i}\}_{i=1}^{M},\alpha_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the set of Pareto-efficient solutions to (<a href="#S2.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ Definition 3 (Coordinated System). ‣ II-B Coordinated Multi-Agent Systems ‣ II Background. Constrained Multi-Objective Optimization in Coordinated Systems ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="S8.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcup_{\mu\in\mathcal{W}_{M}^{+}}S(\mu)=X_{E}(\{f^{i}\}_{i=1}^{M},\alpha_{t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcup_{\mu\in\mathcal{W}_{M}^{+}}S(\mu)=X_{E}(\{f^{i}\}_{i=1}^{M},\alpha_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS2.8" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S8.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Notice that since each <math id="S8.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is assumed to be concave, and the feasible set in (<a href="#S2.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ Definition 3 (Coordinated System). ‣ II-B Coordinated Multi-Agent Systems ‣ II Background. Constrained Multi-Objective Optimization in Coordinated Systems ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) is convex, by (<a href="#S2.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ II-A Multi-Objective Optimization ‣ II Background. Constrained Multi-Objective Optimization in Coordinated Systems ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) there exists <math id="S8.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{W}_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{W}_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\beta^{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}\in X_{E}(\{f^{i}\}_{i=1}^{M},\alpha_{t})\Rightarrow\{\beta^{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}\in S(\mu)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\beta^{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}\in X_{E}(\{f^{i}\}_{i=1}^{M},\alpha_{t})\Rightarrow\{\beta^{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}\in S(\mu)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Now notice that if this <math id="S8.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is always strictly positive, i.e., <math id="S8.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{W}_{M}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{W}_{M}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, then (<a href="#S8.E40" title="Equation 40 ‣ Lemma 1. ‣ VIII-B Lemma 1 Statement and Proof ‣ VIII Appendix ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a>) holds. So now we show <math id="S8.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}^{j}&gt;0\Rightarrow\mu^{j}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}^{j}&gt;0\Rightarrow\mu^{j}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>
Suppose <math id="S8.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{j}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="S8.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\beta_{t}^{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\beta_{t}^{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}^{\top}(\sum_{i=1}^{M}\beta_{t}^{i})\leq p^{*}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}^{\top}(\sum_{i=1}^{M}\beta_{t}^{i})\leq p^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="S8.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}^{j}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}^{j}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}^{\top}(\sum_{i=1}^{M}\beta_{t}^{i})=\alpha_{t}(\sum_{i\neq j}\beta_{t}^{i})+\alpha_{t}(\beta_{t}^{j})\leq p^{*}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}^{\top}(\sum_{i=1}^{M}\beta_{t}^{i})=\alpha_{t}(\sum_{i\neq j}\beta_{t}^{i})+\alpha_{t}(\beta_{t}^{j})\leq p^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{M}\mu^{i}f^{i}(\beta_{t}^{i})=\sum_{i=1,i\neq j}^{M}\mu^{i}f^{i}(\beta_{t}^{i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{M}\mu^{i}f^{i}(\beta_{t}^{i})=\sum_{i=1,i\neq j}^{M}\mu^{i}f^{i}(\beta_{t}^{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS2.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">and since <math id="S8.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S8.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}^{j}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}^{j}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S8.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exists\ \delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">∃</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exists\ \delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}^{\top}(\sum_{i=1,i\neq j}^{M}\beta_{t}^{i})\leq p^{*}-\delta" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}^{\top}(\sum_{i=1,i\neq j}^{M}\beta_{t}^{i})\leq p^{*}-\delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{j}(\alpha_{t},p^{*}):=\{\{\beta_{t}^{i}\}_{i\neq j}:\alpha_{t}(\sum_{i=1,i\neq j}^{M}\beta_{t}^{i})\leq p^{*}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{j}(\alpha_{t},p^{*}):=\{\{\beta_{t}^{i}\}_{i\neq j}:\alpha_{t}(\sum_{i=1,i\neq j}^{M}\beta_{t}^{i})\leq p^{*}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">, and fix some <math id="S8.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}^{k},k\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}^{k},k\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>. we have that</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}^{k}\leq f^{k^{-1}}\left(\frac{1}{\mu^{k}}(p^{*}-\delta-\sum_{i\neq k}\mu^{i}f^{i}(\beta_{t}^{i}))\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}^{k}\leq f^{k^{-1}}\left(\frac{1}{\mu^{k}}(p^{*}-\delta-\sum_{i\neq k}\mu^{i}f^{i}(\beta_{t}^{i}))\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Now take</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\beta_{t}}^{k}=f^{k^{-1}}\left(\frac{1}{\mu^{k}}(p^{*}-\sum_{i\neq k}\mu^{i}f^{i}(\beta_{t}^{i}))\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\beta_{t}}^{k}=f^{k^{-1}}\left(\frac{1}{\mu^{k}}(p^{*}-\sum_{i\neq k}\mu^{i}f^{i}(\beta_{t}^{i}))\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Then, since <math id="S8.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is monotone increasing, we have</span></p>
<table id="S8.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{\beta_{t}}^{k}&gt;\beta_{t}^{k},so" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{\beta_{t}}^{k}&gt;\beta_{t}^{k},so</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S8.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{M}\mu^{i}f^{i}(\beta_{t}^{i})&lt;\sum_{i=1,i\neq k}^{M}\mu^{i}f^{i}(\beta_{t}^{i})+\mu^{k}f^{k}(\bar{\beta_{t}}^{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{M}\mu^{i}f^{i}(\beta_{t}^{i})&lt;\sum_{i=1,i\neq k}^{M}\mu^{i}f^{i}(\beta_{t}^{i})+\mu^{k}f^{k}(\bar{\beta_{t}}^{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS2.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS2.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\beta_{t}^{i}\}_{i=1,i\neq k}^{M}\cup\{\bar{\beta_{t}}^{k}\}\in X_{j}(\alpha_{t},p^{*})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\beta_{t}^{i}\}_{i=1,i\neq k}^{M}\cup\{\bar{\beta_{t}}^{k}\}\in X_{j}(\alpha_{t},p^{*})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS2.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS2.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">so</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\beta_{t}^{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}\notin\arg\max_{\{\gamma^{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\mu^{i}f^{i}(\gamma^{i})\ s.t.\ \alpha_{t}^{\top}(\sum_{i=1}^{M}\gamma^{i}\leq p^{*})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mprescripts></mprescripts><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.667em">.</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\beta_{t}^{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}\notin\arg\max_{\{\gamma^{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\mu^{i}f^{i}(\gamma^{i})\ s.t.\ \alpha_{t}^{\top}(\sum_{i=1}^{M}\gamma^{i}\leq p^{*})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS2.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS2.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">and thus by contradiction we have that for any <math id="S8.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{j},\beta_{t}^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{j},\beta_{t}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S8.E47" title="Equation 47 ‣ VIII-E2 Extracting a Revealed Preference Bound ‣ VIII-E Multi-Target Filtering: Joint Probabilistic Data Association Filter ‣ VIII Appendix ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>), we have <math id="S8.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{j}=0\Rightarrow\beta_{t}^{j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{j}=0\Rightarrow\beta_{t}^{j}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that this directly implies <math id="S8.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}^{j}&gt;0\Rightarrow\mu^{j}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}^{j}&gt;0\Rightarrow\mu^{j}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and so we are done.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S8.SS3.6" class="ltx_text">VIII-C</span> </span><span id="S8.SS3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ III-B Type-I Error Minimizing Statistical Detector ‣ III Result 1. Statistical Detection of Pareto-Efficient Coordination ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></span></h3>

<div id="S8.SS3.8" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof: 1.</h6>
<div id="S8.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose <math id="S8.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> holds. By Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ III-A1 Testing Pareto-Efficiency ‣ III-A Main Result 1A. Linear Programming Formulation for Detection of Deterministic Pareto-Efficient Coordination. ‣ III Result 1. Statistical Detection of Pareto-Efficient Coordination ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <math id="S8.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to (<a href="#S3.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ Item 2 ‣ Theorem 1. ‣ III-A1 Testing Pareto-Efficiency ‣ III-A Main Result 1A. Linear Programming Formulation for Detection of Deterministic Pareto-Efficient Coordination. ‣ III Result 1. Statistical Detection of Pareto-Efficient Coordination ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>) having a feasible solution. Let <math id="S8.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bar{u}_{t}^{i},\bar{\lambda}_{t}^{i},t\in[T])_{i=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bar{u}_{t}^{i},\bar{\lambda}_{t}^{i},t\in[T])_{i=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> denote a feasible solution to (<a href="#S3.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ Item 2 ‣ Theorem 1. ‣ III-A1 Testing Pareto-Efficiency ‣ III-A Main Result 1A. Linear Programming Formulation for Detection of Deterministic Pareto-Efficient Coordination. ‣ III Result 1. Statistical Detection of Pareto-Efficient Coordination ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>). Then substituting <math id="S8.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\beta}^{i}_{t}=\beta^{i}_{t}-\epsilon^{i}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\beta}^{i}_{t}=\beta^{i}_{t}-\epsilon^{i}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, it is apparent that (<math id="S8.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{u}_{t}^{i},\bar{\lambda}_{t}^{i},\Phi=\Psi^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{u}_{t}^{i},\bar{\lambda}_{t}^{i},\Phi=\Psi^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>) is feasible. So, clearly the minimizing solution of (<a href="#S3.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ III-B Type-I Error Minimizing Statistical Detector ‣ III Result 1. Statistical Detection of Pareto-Efficient Coordination ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) satisfies <math id="S8.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\Phi}^{i}(\tilde{\mathcal{D}})\leq\Psi^{i}\ \forall i\in[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\Phi}^{i}(\tilde{\mathcal{D}})\leq\Psi^{i}\ \forall i\in[M]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS3.9" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof: 2.</h6>
<div id="S8.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">First note that</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bigcap_{i}\{\hat{\Phi}^{i}(\tilde{\mathcal{D}})\leq\Psi^{i}\}\subseteq\{\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}})\leq\Psi\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcap_{i}\{\hat{\Phi}^{i}(\tilde{\mathcal{D}})\leq\Psi^{i}\}\subseteq\{\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}})\leq\Psi\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then from (<a href="#S3.E18" title="Equation 18 ‣ Item 1 ‣ Theorem 2. ‣ III-B Type-I Error Minimizing Statistical Detector ‣ III Result 1. Statistical Detection of Pareto-Efficient Coordination ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>), observe that</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{H_{0}\}=\{H_{0}\}\bigcap\{\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}})\leq\Psi\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">⋂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{H_{0}\}=\{H_{0}\}\bigcap\{\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}})\leq\Psi\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Then the probability of Type-I error is</span></p>
<table id="S8.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\mathbb{P}_{\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}})}(H_{1}|H_{0})\\
&amp;\quad=\mathbb{P}(\bar{F}_{\Psi}(\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}}))\leq\gamma\ |\{H_{0}\}\bigcap\{\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}})\leq\Psi\})\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mphantom></mphantom></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="1.000em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>H</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">}</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\mathbb{P}_{\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}})}(H_{1}|H_{0})\\
&amp;\quad=\mathbb{P}(\bar{F}_{\Psi}(\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}}))\leq\gamma\ |\{H_{0}\}\bigcap\{\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}})\leq\Psi\})\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS3.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Now if <math id="S8.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}})=\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}})=\Psi</annotation></semantics></math>, then since <math id="S8.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{F}_{\Psi}(\Psi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{F}_{\Psi}(\Psi)</annotation></semantics></math> is uniform
in [0,1] we have <math id="S8.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}})}(H_{1}|H_{0})=\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}})}(H_{1}|H_{0})=\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="S8.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}})&lt;\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}})&lt;\Psi</annotation></semantics></math> then</span></p>
<table id="S8.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\bar{F}_{\Psi}(\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}}))\geq\bar{F}_{\Psi}(\Psi)\\
&amp;\quad\Rightarrow\mathbb{P}(\bar{F}_{\Psi}(\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}}))\leq\gamma)\leq\mathbb{P}(\bar{F}_{\Psi}(\Psi)\leq\gamma)\leq\gamma\\
&amp;\quad\Rightarrow\mathbb{P}_{\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}})}(H_{1}|H_{0})\leq\gamma\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\bar{F}_{\Psi}(\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}}))\geq\bar{F}_{\Psi}(\Psi)\\
&amp;\quad\Rightarrow\mathbb{P}(\bar{F}_{\Psi}(\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}}))\leq\gamma)\leq\mathbb{P}(\bar{F}_{\Psi}(\Psi)\leq\gamma)\leq\gamma\\
&amp;\quad\Rightarrow\mathbb{P}_{\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}})}(H_{1}|H_{0})\leq\gamma\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS3.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS3.10" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof: 3.</h6>
<div id="S8.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose <math id="S8.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Phi}^{i}(\tilde{\mathcal{D}})&gt;\hat{\Phi}^{i}(\tilde{\mathcal{D}})\ \forall i\in[M]\Rightarrow\bar{\Phi}^{*}(\tilde{\mathcal{D}}):=\max_{i}\bar{\Phi}^{i}(\tilde{\mathcal{D}})&gt;\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.667em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Phi}^{i}(\tilde{\mathcal{D}})&gt;\hat{\Phi}^{i}(\tilde{\mathcal{D}})\ \forall i\in[M]\Rightarrow\bar{\Phi}^{*}(\tilde{\mathcal{D}}):=\max_{i}\bar{\Phi}^{i}(\tilde{\mathcal{D}})&gt;\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have</span></p>
<table id="S8.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\mathbb{P}(\bar{F}_{\Psi}(\bar{\Phi}^{*}(\tilde{\mathcal{D}}))\leq\gamma|\bigcap_{i}\{\bar{\Phi}^{i}(\tilde{\mathcal{D}})\leq\Psi^{i}\})\\
&amp;\geq P(\bar{F}_{\Psi}(\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}}))\leq\gamma|\bigcap_{i}\{\hat{\Phi}^{i}(\tilde{\mathcal{D}})\leq\Psi^{i}\}\\
&amp;\Rightarrow\mathbb{P}_{\bar{\Phi}(\tilde{\mathcal{D}})}(H_{1}|H_{0})\geq\mathbb{P}_{\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}})}(H_{1}|H_{0})\ \forall\bar{\Phi}\in[\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}}),\Psi]\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="1.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\mathbb{P}(\bar{F}_{\Psi}(\bar{\Phi}^{*}(\tilde{\mathcal{D}}))\leq\gamma|\bigcap_{i}\{\bar{\Phi}^{i}(\tilde{\mathcal{D}})\leq\Psi^{i}\})\\
&amp;\geq P(\bar{F}_{\Psi}(\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}}))\leq\gamma|\bigcap_{i}\{\hat{\Phi}^{i}(\tilde{\mathcal{D}})\leq\Psi^{i}\}\\
&amp;\Rightarrow\mathbb{P}_{\bar{\Phi}(\tilde{\mathcal{D}})}(H_{1}|H_{0})\geq\mathbb{P}_{\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}})}(H_{1}|H_{0})\ \forall\bar{\Phi}\in[\Phi^{*}(\bar{\bm{\beta}}),\Psi]\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S8.SS4.6" class="ltx_text">VIII-D</span> </span><span id="S8.SS4.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Example Radar Waveform Specifications</span></h3>

<div id="S8.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To give a precise structure to the radar dynamics, the observation noise covariance <math id="S8.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{t}(\alpha_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}(\alpha_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S5.E32" title="Equation 32 ‣ V-B1 Multi-Target Filtering ‣ V-B Deriving the Covertness Bound from Tracking Dynamics ‣ V Extended Example. Detecting and Identifying Pareto-efficient Coordination amongst UAVs ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>) can directly be mapped from particular radar waveforms. Specific waveform examples, along with their noise covariance matrices, are presented here. Further details on maximum likelihood estimation involving the radar ambiguity function can be found in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>]</cite>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The key idea is that by adapting the waveform parameters, the radar can modulate the covariance matrix <math id="S8.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>. This modulation can be viewed at a higher level as an adaptation of the eigenvalues of <math id="S8.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>. We treat <math id="S8.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> as the vector of eigenvalues of <math id="S8.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{-1}(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{-1}(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>, so that increasing <math id="S8.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> increases the measurement precision. Such an increase directly corresponds to, or is enacted by, changes to the physical-layer waveform parametrization, as illustrated above.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Next, given the above Linear Gaussian specification of the multi-target dynamics (<a href="#S5.E31" title="Equation 31 ‣ V-B1 Multi-Target Filtering ‣ V-B Deriving the Covertness Bound from Tracking Dynamics ‣ V Extended Example. Detecting and Identifying Pareto-efficient Coordination amongst UAVs ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>), we present two multi-target filtering examples. The goal is to illustrate how the spectral interpretation of <math id="S8.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S8.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S5.E32" title="Equation 32 ‣ V-B1 Multi-Target Filtering ‣ V-B Deriving the Covertness Bound from Tracking Dynamics ‣ V Extended Example. Detecting and Identifying Pareto-efficient Coordination amongst UAVs ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>) gives rise within these algorithms to the linear constraint <math id="S8.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}(\sum_{i=1}^{M}\beta_{t}^{i})\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}(\sum_{i=1}^{M}\beta_{t}^{i})\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S2.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ Definition 3 (Coordinated System). ‣ II-B Coordinated Multi-Agent Systems ‣ II Background. Constrained Multi-Objective Optimization in Coordinated Systems ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>). Recall that this linear constraint should correspond to a physical-layer bound on the radar’s average measurement precision.
The waveform specifications involve the following terms:</p>
<ul id="S8.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S8.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S8.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S8.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the speed of light (in free space),</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S8.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S8.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the carrier frequency,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S8.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S8.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> is an adjustable parameter in the waveform,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S8.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S8.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is the signal to noise ratio at the radar,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S8.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S8.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=\sqrt{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=\sqrt{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the unit imaginary number,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S8.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S8.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is the complex envelope of the waveform,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S8.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S8.I1.i7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> is the vector of eigenvalues of <math id="S8.I1.i7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S8.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">We now provide three example waveforms and their resulting observation noise covariance matrices <math id="S8.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ol id="S8.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S8.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S8.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Triangular Pulse - Continuous Wave</p>
<table id="S8.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}s(t)&amp;=\begin{cases}\sqrt{\frac{3}{2\theta}}\left(1-\frac{|t|}{\theta}\right)\quad&amp;-\theta&lt;t&lt;\theta\\
0&amp;\textrm{otherwise}\end{cases}\\
R(\alpha)&amp;=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{c^{2}\theta^{2}}{12\eta}&amp;0\\
0&amp;\frac{5c^{2}}{2\omega_{c}^{2}\theta^{2}\eta}\end{bmatrix}\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>θ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}s(t)&amp;=\begin{cases}\sqrt{\frac{3}{2\theta}}\left(1-\frac{|t|}{\theta}\right)\quad&amp;-\theta&lt;t&lt;\theta\\
0&amp;\textrm{otherwise}\end{cases}\\
R(\alpha)&amp;=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{c^{2}\theta^{2}}{12\eta}&amp;0\\
0&amp;\frac{5c^{2}}{2\omega_{c}^{2}\theta^{2}\eta}\end{bmatrix}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S8.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Gaussian Pulse - Continuous Wave</p>
<table id="S8.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}s(t)&amp;=\left(\frac{1}{\pi\theta^{2}}\right)^{1/4}\exp\left(\frac{-t^{2}}{2\theta^{2}}\right)\\
R(\alpha)&amp;=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{c^{2}\theta^{2}}{s\eta}&amp;0\\
0&amp;\frac{c^{2}}{2\omega_{c}^{2}\theta^{2}\eta}\end{bmatrix}\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mfrac><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}s(t)&amp;=\left(\frac{1}{\pi\theta^{2}}\right)^{1/4}\exp\left(\frac{-t^{2}}{2\theta^{2}}\right)\\
R(\alpha)&amp;=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{c^{2}\theta^{2}}{s\eta}&amp;0\\
0&amp;\frac{c^{2}}{2\omega_{c}^{2}\theta^{2}\eta}\end{bmatrix}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S8.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Gaussian Pulse - Linear Frequency Modulation Chirp</p>
<table id="S8.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle s(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle s(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\frac{1}{\pi\theta_{1}^{2}}\right)^{1/4}\exp\left(-\left(\frac{1}{2\theta_{1}^{2}}-j\theta_{2}\right)t^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\frac{1}{\pi\theta_{1}^{2}}\right)^{1/4}\exp\left(-\left(\frac{1}{2\theta_{1}^{2}}-j\theta_{2}\right)t^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S8.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex41.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{c^{2}\theta_{1}^{2}}{2\eta}&amp;\frac{-c^{2}\theta_{2}\theta_{1}^{2}}{\omega_{c}\eta}\\
\frac{-c^{2}\theta_{2}\theta_{1}^{2}}{\omega_{c}\eta}&amp;\frac{c^{2}}{\omega_{c}^{2}\eta}\left(\frac{1}{2\theta_{1}^{2}}+2\theta_{2}^{2}\theta_{1}^{2}\right)\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}\frac{c^{2}\theta_{1}^{2}}{2\eta}&amp;\frac{-c^{2}\theta_{2}\theta_{1}^{2}}{\omega_{c}\eta}\\
\frac{-c^{2}\theta_{2}\theta_{1}^{2}}{\omega_{c}\eta}&amp;\frac{c^{2}}{\omega_{c}^{2}\eta}\left(\frac{1}{2\theta_{1}^{2}}+2\theta_{2}^{2}\theta_{1}^{2}\right)\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S8.SS5.6" class="ltx_text">VIII-E</span> </span><span id="S8.SS5.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Multi-Target Filtering: Joint Probabilistic Data Association Filter</span></h3>

<div id="S8.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The joint probabilistic data association filter (JPDAF) operates under the regime where <math id="S8.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> measurements <math id="S8.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{k}^{j},j\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{k}^{j},j\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#S5.E31" title="Equation 31 ‣ V-B1 Multi-Target Filtering ‣ V-B Deriving the Covertness Bound from Tracking Dynamics ‣ V Extended Example. Detecting and Identifying Pareto-efficient Coordination amongst UAVs ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>) of <math id="S8.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> targets are obtained, and it is not known which measurements correspond to which target. See <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>]</cite> for clarification of any details.</p>
</div>
<section id="S8.SS5.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S8.SS5.SSS1.6" class="ltx_text">VIII-E</span>1 </span>Filter Dynamics</h4>

<div id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define the empirical validation matrix <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Omega=[\omega_{jt},j\in[n],t\in\{0,\dots,m\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega=[\omega_{jt},j\in[n],t\in\{0,\dots,m\}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{jt}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{jt}=1</annotation></semantics></math> if measurement <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> is in the <span id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">validation gate</span> of target <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise. It is common to let the <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math> index correspond to "none of the targets".</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Now we construct an object <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> known as the "joint association event", as</p>
<table id="S8.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta=\bigcap_{j=1}^{m}\theta_{jt_{j}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta=\bigcap_{j=1}^{m}\theta_{jt_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<ul id="S8.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S8.I3.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">-</span> 
<div id="S8.I3.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I3.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S8.I3.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{jt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{jt}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the event that measurement <math id="S8.I3.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> originated from target <math id="S8.I3.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I3.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">-</span> 
<div id="S8.I3.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I3.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S8.I3.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is the index of the target which measurement <math id="S8.I3.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> is associated with in the event under consideration</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">So, <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> can represent any possible set of associations between measurements and targets.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Then, we can form the <span id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">event matrix</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\Omega}(\theta)=[\hat{\omega}_{jt}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\Omega}(\theta)=[\hat{\omega}_{jt}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="S8.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\omega}_{jt}=\begin{cases}1,\,\theta_{jt}\in\theta\\
0,\,\textrm{else}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mtext>else</mtext></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\omega}_{jt}=\begin{cases}1,\,\theta_{jt}\in\theta\\
0,\,\textrm{else}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\Omega}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\Omega}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is thus the indicator matrix of measurement-target associations in event <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We say an event <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> is a <span id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">feasible association event</span> if</p>
<ol id="S8.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S8.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S8.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">a measurement is associated to only one source,</p>
<table id="S8.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t=0}^{m}\hat{\omega}_{jt}(\theta)=1,\quad\forall\,j\in[n]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t=0}^{m}\hat{\omega}_{jt}(\theta)=1,\quad\forall\,j\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S8.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">at most one measurement originates from each target,</p>
<table id="S8.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{t}(\theta):=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\hat{\omega}_{jt}(\theta)\leq 1,\quad\forall\,t\in[m]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{t}(\theta):=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\hat{\omega}_{jt}(\theta)\leq 1,\quad\forall\,t\in[m]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Denote by <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> the set of all feasible events.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The binary variable <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{t}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{t}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is known as the "target detection indicator" since it indicates whether, in event <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, a measurement <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> has been associated to target <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. We may also define a "measurement association indicator"</p>
<table id="S8.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{j}(\theta):=\sum_{t=1}^{m}\hat{\omega}_{jt}(\theta)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{j}(\theta):=\sum_{t=1}^{m}\hat{\omega}_{jt}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">which indicates if a particular measurement <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> is associated with a target <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Note the difference between (<a href="#S8.E44" title="Equation 44 ‣ VIII-E1 Filter Dynamics ‣ VIII-E Multi-Target Filtering: Joint Probabilistic Data Association Filter ‣ VIII Appendix ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>) and (<a href="#S8.E42" title="Equation 42 ‣ Item 1 ‣ VIII-E1 Filter Dynamics ‣ VIII-E Multi-Target Filtering: Joint Probabilistic Data Association Filter ‣ VIII Appendix ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>); the latter sums from <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> to include the possibility of a measurement being assigned to "no target", i.e., clutter, while the former sums from <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, indicating if the measurement has been assigned to an actual target.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Using these definitions we can write the number of false (unassociated) measurements in event <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="S8.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(\theta):=\sum_{j=1}^{n}[1-\tau_{j}(\theta)]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\theta):=\sum_{j=1}^{n}[1-\tau_{j}(\theta)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Using these preliminary concepts, the JPDAF can be formulated by first deriving the posterior probability of joint-association events given the measured data, then incorporating this into a standard filtering scheme akin to the Kalman filter. The filtering can be done in an uncoupled or coupled manner; the former assumes target measurements are independently distributed, and the latter is capable of correlations in target state estimation errors.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Uncoupled Filtering</span>: Now given a particular feasible joint-association event <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}\in\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}\in\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>, and letting <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{t},\tau_{j},\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{t},\tau_{j},\phi</annotation></semantics></math> be shorthand for (<a href="#S8.E43" title="Equation 43 ‣ Item 2 ‣ VIII-E1 Filter Dynamics ‣ VIII-E Multi-Target Filtering: Joint Probabilistic Data Association Filter ‣ VIII Appendix ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>), (<a href="#S8.E44" title="Equation 44 ‣ VIII-E1 Filter Dynamics ‣ VIII-E Multi-Target Filtering: Joint Probabilistic Data Association Filter ‣ VIII Appendix ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>), (<a href="#S8.E45" title="Equation 45 ‣ VIII-E1 Filter Dynamics ‣ VIII-E Multi-Target Filtering: Joint Probabilistic Data Association Filter ‣ VIII Appendix ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a>), respectively evaluated at <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>]</cite> derives the posterior probability <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(\theta_{k}|\{y_{k}^{j}\}_{j=1}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(\theta_{k}|\{y_{k}^{j}\}_{j=1}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math>, under the uncoupled assumption, as</p>
<table id="S8.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;P(\theta_{k}|\{y_{k}^{j}\}_{j=1}^{n})\\
&amp;\propto\frac{\phi!}{m_{k}!}\mu_{F}(\phi)V^{-\phi}\prod_{j}[f_{tj}(y_{k}^{j})]^{\tau_{j}}\prod_{t}(P^{t}_{D})^{\delta_{t}}(1-P^{t}_{D})^{1-\delta_{t}}\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mphantom></mphantom></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mi>j</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mi>t</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;P(\theta_{k}|\{y_{k}^{j}\}_{j=1}^{n})\\
&amp;\propto\frac{\phi!}{m_{k}!}\mu_{F}(\phi)V^{-\phi}\prod_{j}[f_{tj}(y_{k}^{j})]^{\tau_{j}}\prod_{t}(P^{t}_{D})^{\delta_{t}}(1-P^{t}_{D})^{1-\delta_{t}}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{D}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{D}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the detection probability of target <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{k}=n-\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{k}=n-\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, and</p>
<table id="S8.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{tj}(y_{k}^{j})=\mathcal{N}(y_{k}^{j};\hat{y}^{t_{j}}_{k|k-1},S^{t_{j}}_{k})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{tj}(y_{k}^{j})=\mathcal{N}(y_{k}^{j};\hat{y}^{t_{j}}_{k|k-1},S^{t_{j}}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p8.3" class="ltx_p">with <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}^{t_{j}}_{k|k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}^{t_{j}}_{k|k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> the predicted measurement for target <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> in the previous iteration of the filter, and <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{t_{j}}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{t_{j}}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> the associated innovation covariance matrix. <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{F}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{F}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> is the probability mass function governing the number of false measurements <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, and such measurements not associated with a target are assumed uniformly distributed in the surveillance region of volume <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Given, this posterior probability the uncoupled filter proceeds by separately filtering each target state independently. For brevity we do not introduce this filtering process, but do so for the more sophisticated and robust <span id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">coupled</span> filter.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Coupled Filtering</span>:
Given a particular feasible joint-association event <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}\in\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}\in\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>, and letting <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{t},\tau_{j},\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{t},\tau_{j},\phi</annotation></semantics></math> be shorthand for (<a href="#S8.E43" title="Equation 43 ‣ Item 2 ‣ VIII-E1 Filter Dynamics ‣ VIII-E Multi-Target Filtering: Joint Probabilistic Data Association Filter ‣ VIII Appendix ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>), (<a href="#S8.E44" title="Equation 44 ‣ VIII-E1 Filter Dynamics ‣ VIII-E Multi-Target Filtering: Joint Probabilistic Data Association Filter ‣ VIII Appendix ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>), (<a href="#S8.E45" title="Equation 45 ‣ VIII-E1 Filter Dynamics ‣ VIII-E Multi-Target Filtering: Joint Probabilistic Data Association Filter ‣ VIII Appendix ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a>), respectively evaluated at <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>]</cite> derives the posterior probability <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(\theta_{k}|\{y_{k}^{j}\}_{j=1}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(\theta_{k}|\{y_{k}^{j}\}_{j=1}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="S8.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;P(\theta_{k}|\{y_{k}^{j}\}_{j=1}^{n})\propto\frac{\phi!}{m_{k}!}\mu_{F}(\phi)V^{-\phi}f_{t_{j_{1}},t_{j_{2}},\dots}(y_{k}^{j},j:\tau_{j}=1)\\
&amp;\prod_{t}(P^{t}_{D})^{\delta_{t}}(1-P^{t}_{D})^{1-\delta_{t}}\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∝</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>V</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mi>t</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;P(\theta_{k}|\{y_{k}^{j}\}_{j=1}^{n})\propto\frac{\phi!}{m_{k}!}\mu_{F}(\phi)V^{-\phi}f_{t_{j_{1}},t_{j_{2}},\dots}(y_{k}^{j},j:\tau_{j}=1)\\
&amp;\prod_{t}(P^{t}_{D})^{\delta_{t}}(1-P^{t}_{D})^{1-\delta_{t}}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p10.2" class="ltx_p">where here <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{t_{j_{1}},t_{j_{2}},\dots}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t_{j_{1}},t_{j_{2}},\dots}</annotation></semantics></math> is the joint pdf of the measurements of the targets under consideration, and <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{j_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{j_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the target which <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{k}^{j_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{k}^{j_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> is associated in event <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Now we introduce the Joint Probabilistic Data Association Coupled Filter (JPDACF) state estimation and covariance update.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">We form the stacked state vector of predicted states, and associated covariance, as</p>
<table id="S8.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}_{k|k-1}=\begin{bmatrix}\hat{x}^{1}_{k|k-1}\\
\vdots\\
\hat{x}^{m}_{k|k-1}\end{bmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}_{k|k-1}=\begin{bmatrix}\hat{x}^{1}_{k|k-1}\\
\vdots\\
\hat{x}^{m}_{k|k-1}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S8.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{k|k-1}=\begin{bmatrix}P^{1\,1}_{k|k-1}\,\dots\,P^{1\,m}_{k|k-1}\\
P^{m\,1}_{k|k-1}\,\dots\,P^{m\,m}_{k|k-1}\end{bmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mn>1 1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn> 1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{k|k-1}=\begin{bmatrix}P^{1\,1}_{k|k-1}\,\dots\,P^{1\,m}_{k|k-1}\\
P^{m\,1}_{k|k-1}\,\dots\,P^{m\,m}_{k|k-1}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{t_{1}\,t_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{t_{1}\,t_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the cross-covariance between targets <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. The coupled filtering is done as follows:</p>
<table id="S8.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{x}_{k|k}=\hat{x}_{k|k-1}+W_{k}\sum_{\theta}P(\theta|\{y_{k}^{j}\}_{j=1}^{n})[\bm{y}_{k}(\theta)-\hat{y}_{k|k-1}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>θ</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{x}_{k|k}=\hat{x}_{k|k-1}+W_{k}\sum_{\theta}P(\theta|\{y_{k}^{j}\}_{j=1}^{n})[\bm{y}_{k}(\theta)-\hat{y}_{k|k-1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p13.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="S8.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}_{k}(\theta)=\begin{bmatrix}y_{k}^{j_{1}(\theta)}\\
\vdots\\
y_{k}^{j_{m}(\theta)}\end{bmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}_{k}(\theta)=\begin{bmatrix}y_{k}^{j_{1}(\theta)}\\
\vdots\\
y_{k}^{j_{m}(\theta)}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p13.3" class="ltx_p">and <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{i}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{i}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is the measurement associated with target <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> in event <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>. The filter gain <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="S8.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{k}=P_{k|k-1}\hat{C}_{k}^{\top}\left[\hat{C}_{k}P_{k|k-1}\hat{C}_{k}^{\top}+\hat{R}_{k}\right]^{-1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{k}=P_{k|k-1}\hat{C}_{k}^{\top}\left[\hat{C}_{k}P_{k|k-1}\hat{C}_{k}^{\top}+\hat{R}_{k}\right]^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p13.4" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="S8.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{C}_{k}=\textrm{diag}\left[\delta_{1}(\theta)C_{k}^{1},\dots,\delta_{m}(\theta)C_{k}^{m}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{C}_{k}=\textrm{diag}\left[\delta_{1}(\theta)C_{k}^{1},\dots,\delta_{m}(\theta)C_{k}^{m}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S8.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{R}_{k}=\textrm{diag}\left[R_{k}^{1},\dots,R_{k}^{m}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{R}_{k}=\textrm{diag}\left[R_{k}^{1},\dots,R_{k}^{m}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p13.5" class="ltx_p">are the block diagonal measurement and noise covariance matrices. The binary detection indicator variables <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{i}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{i}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> accounts for the possibility of a measurement not being associated to target <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. The predicted stacked measurement vector is</p>
<table id="S8.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{k|k-1}=\hat{C}_{k}\hat{x}_{k|k-1}=\hat{C}_{k}\hat{A}_{k-1}\hat{x}_{k-1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{k|k-1}=\hat{C}_{k}\hat{x}_{k|k-1}=\hat{C}_{k}\hat{A}_{k-1}\hat{x}_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p13.6" class="ltx_p">with <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}_{k-1}=\textrm{diag}[A_{k-1}^{1},\dots,A_{k-1}^{m}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}_{k-1}=\textrm{diag}[A_{k-1}^{1},\dots,A_{k-1}^{m}]</annotation></semantics></math> the block diagonal state update matrix.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p14.1" class="ltx_p">The covariance of the updated state is given as</p>
<table id="S8.E46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{k|k}=P_{k|k-1}+[1-\psi_{0}]W_{k}\hat{S}_{k}W_{k}^{\top}+\tilde{P}_{k}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{k|k}=P_{k|k-1}+[1-\psi_{0}]W_{k}\hat{S}_{k}W_{k}^{\top}+\tilde{P}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p14.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{S}_{k}=\hat{C}_{k}P_{k|k-1}\hat{C}_{k}^{\top}+\hat{R}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{S}_{k}=\hat{C}_{k}P_{k|k-1}\hat{C}_{k}^{\top}+\hat{R}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the innovation covariance,</p>
<table id="S8.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\psi_{jt}:=\sum_{\theta:\theta_{jt}\in\theta}P(\theta|\{y_{k}^{j}\}_{j=1}^{n})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{jt}:=\sum_{\theta:\theta_{jt}\in\theta}P(\theta|\{y_{k}^{j}\}_{j=1}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p14.3" class="ltx_p">and <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{0}:=\sum_{j=1}^{m}\psi_{j0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{0}:=\sum_{j=1}^{m}\psi_{j0}</annotation></semantics></math> is the probability that no measurements arise from targets. <math id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{P}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{P}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the spread of the innovation terms:</p>
<table id="S8.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{P}_{k}:=W_{k}\tilde{S}_{k}W_{k}^{\top}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{P}_{k}:=W_{k}\tilde{S}_{k}W_{k}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p14.4" class="ltx_p">with</p>
<table id="S8.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{S}_{k}=\begin{bmatrix}\sum_{j=1}^{m_{k}}\psi_{j1}\left[y_{k}^{1}-\hat{x}^{1}_{k|k-1}\right]\\
\cdot\left[y_{k}^{1}-\hat{x}^{1}_{k|k-1}\right]^{\top}-\nu_{1,k}\nu_{1,k}^{\top}\\
\vdots\\
\sum_{j=1}^{m_{k}}\psi_{jm}\left[y_{k}^{m}-\hat{x}^{m}_{k|k-1}\right]\\
\cdot\left[y_{k}^{m}-\hat{x}^{m}_{k|k-1}\right]^{\top}-\nu_{m,k}\nu_{m,k}^{\top}\end{bmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{S}_{k}=\begin{bmatrix}\sum_{j=1}^{m_{k}}\psi_{j1}\left[y_{k}^{1}-\hat{x}^{1}_{k|k-1}\right]\\
\cdot\left[y_{k}^{1}-\hat{x}^{1}_{k|k-1}\right]^{\top}-\nu_{1,k}\nu_{1,k}^{\top}\\
\vdots\\
\sum_{j=1}^{m_{k}}\psi_{jm}\left[y_{k}^{m}-\hat{x}^{m}_{k|k-1}\right]\\
\cdot\left[y_{k}^{m}-\hat{x}^{m}_{k|k-1}\right]^{\top}-\nu_{m,k}\nu_{m,k}^{\top}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS1.p14.5" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="S8.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{i,k}=\sum_{j=1}^{m_{k}}\psi_{ji}\left[y_{k}^{i}-\hat{x}^{i}_{k|k-1}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{i,k}=\sum_{j=1}^{m_{k}}\psi_{ji}\left[y_{k}^{i}-\hat{x}^{i}_{k|k-1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8.SS5.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S8.SS5.SSS2.6" class="ltx_text">VIII-E</span>2 </span>Extracting a Revealed Preference Bound</h4>

<div id="S8.SS5.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The crucial observation is that, as in the Kalman filter algebraic Riccati equation (<a href="#S5.E33" title="Equation 33 ‣ V-B2 Deriving the Linear Spectral Constraint ‣ V-B Deriving the Covertness Bound from Tracking Dynamics ‣ V Extended Example. Detecting and Identifying Pareto-efficient Coordination amongst UAVs ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>), the covariance (<a href="#S8.E46" title="Equation 46 ‣ VIII-E1 Filter Dynamics ‣ VIII-E Multi-Target Filtering: Joint Probabilistic Data Association Filter ‣ VIII Appendix ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">46</span></a>) is monotone decreasing in <math id="S8.SS5.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S8.SS5.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, since this corresponds to increasing <math id="S8.SS5.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{R}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{R}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for fixed <math id="S8.SS5.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the asymptotic measurement precision (inverse of asymptotic predicted covariance) is monotone <span id="S8.SS5.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">non-decreasing</span> in <math id="S8.SS5.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and by the same reasoning as Lemma 3 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>, we may derive the equivalence</p>
<table id="S8.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{M}\beta_{t}^{i}\right)\leq 1\Longleftrightarrow\lim_{k\to\infty}P_{k|k}^{-1}(\alpha_{t},\{\beta_{t}^{i}\})\leq\hat{P}^{-1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.1389em" stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{M}\beta_{t}^{i}\right)\leq 1\Longleftrightarrow\lim_{k\to\infty}P_{k|k}^{-1}(\alpha_{t},\{\beta_{t}^{i}\})\leq\hat{P}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, we again have that the constraint <math id="S8.SS5.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{M}\beta_{t}^{i}\right)\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{M}\beta_{t}^{i}\right)\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> is a natural representation for a bound on the average measurement precision.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS5.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Without loss of generality, we can take <math id="S8.SS5.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}^{i}&gt;0\ \forall t\in[T],i\in[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.667em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}^{i}&gt;0\ \forall t\in[T],i\in[M]</annotation></semantics></math>. Then by Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ VIII-B Lemma 1 Statement and Proof ‣ VIII Appendix ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> in Appendix A, (<a href="#S2.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ Definition 3 (Coordinated System). ‣ II-B Coordinated Multi-Agent Systems ‣ II Background. Constrained Multi-Objective Optimization in Coordinated Systems ‣ Multi-Agent Inverse RL for Identifying Pareto-Efficient Coordination – Distributionally Robust Approach" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) is equivalent to</p>
<table id="S8.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\{\beta_{t}^{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}\in&amp;\arg\max_{\{\beta^{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\mu^{i}f^{i}(\beta^{i})\ \ s.t.\ \alpha_{t}^{\top}(\sum_{i=1}^{M}\beta^{i})\leq 1\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mmultiscripts><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mprescripts></mprescripts><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mstyle><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2.000em;" width="2.000em"></mspace><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="1.167em">.</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\{\beta_{t}^{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}\in&amp;\arg\max_{\{\beta^{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\mu^{i}f^{i}(\beta^{i})\ \ s.t.\ \alpha_{t}^{\top}(\sum_{i=1}^{M}\beta^{i})\leq 1\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">for any <math id="S8.SS5.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathcal{W}_{M}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathcal{W}_{M}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS5.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS5.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that we are interested in the <span id="S8.SS5.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">inverse</span> multi-objective optimization problem; in the following section we provide a necessary and sufficient condition for the existence of objective functions for which the observed signals <math id="S8.SS5.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\beta_{t}^{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\beta_{t}^{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy constrained multi-objective optimization.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
